  "source_MD5_rule": "Before raw source events, recheck ORIGINAL provider UUID, byte count, MD5 and exact source taxon registration from pre-existing SHA-frozen source-only metadata. Verify downloaded original bytes MD5, then replay old one_taxon q and daylength mean/n before doing month model. No source substitution. Any mismatch is SOURCE_HOLD.",
  "baseline_replay_tolerance": 1e-10,
  "original_q": "Original one exact timestamp-nearest UTC hourly GPS fix per tag, successive 0.5-2h valid great-circle displacement <=60kmh, same solar date/daypart at start/midpoint/end, >=3 qualified day and night segments per original tagged date, >=10 original qualified dates per tagged year, original tag-equal q and within-tag/year q~local daylength, bootstrap only if >=5 original tags. These effects must replay unchanged.",
  "new_primary": "For each ORIGINAL tag-year with >=10 q-qualified solar dates, calculate q/date and local astronomical daylength from the same source GPS and define group=original tag x calendar year x calendar month. A qualifying group has >=5 distinct q-qualified dates AND within-group daylength range >=0.05h. Tag-year month-FE slope = sum within-group centered (L-meanL)(q-meanq) / sum within-group centered (L-meanL)^2 across qualified groups, only if >=2 qualified months, >=10 qualified dates, and >=0.05 h² sum of centered daylength squares. Tag's slope = equal mean over its qualifying original years. Source native effect is equal mean across qualifying original tags, only if >=5 independent qualified tags; 2000 resamples of original TAG IDs, bootstrap percentile 95 interval. No raw individual effects exported.",
  "new_reference_lat_sensitivity": "On SAME q-qualified dates and qualified month groups as primary, replace local daylength with source-median tagged-mean latitude fixed over dates. This removes within-month changes in geodetic latitude from the astronomical daylength covariate, without removing nonastronomical seasonal factors. Source reference latitude and date never exported.",
  "comparability_constraints": "All 5 source original registered taxa retained; no species or source selected by new conditioned q sign. Baseline original full-year effect sample NOT equal to month-qualified sample; compare observational direction and support only, not a formal test of difference or cause. Distinct published DOI not proof of distinct tags or populations. Study seasons and GPS duty cycles may differ.",
  "reporting": "Only per original source and registered target native taxon: q/daylength baseline replay yes/no, source quality counts and months, count qualified independent original tags, month-adjusted tag-equal slope/nominal 95 interval, optional fixed-lat sensitivity, and explicit HOLD. No original GPS rows/individual IDs/coordinates/precise dates/individual effects or bootstrap draws leave the ephemeral Action runner.",
  "inference_limit": "Postoutcome seasonal method sensitivity on two prior target species; both the source targets and method were selected after viewing full-year positive q/daylength results. This is NOT a preregistered test of photoperiod, latitudinal adaptation, or general global temporal niche. Year-month FE alone cannot control day-of-month changing weather, migration timing, breeding or sampling schedule.",
  "legacy_48_sunlight_heading_external_replicated": false,
  "legacy_12_ERA5_raw_SHA_HOLD": true
